<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
As a few of you might know I was kinda getting burned out trying to level Leat.  Most of it was because I was shooting for the hate raid but missed out.  (Came darn close though.)  Well one way for me to cure this was to take a break from killing stuff and work on some trade skills.<P>This worked out very well for me as I have a bunch of Masters now.  (Fishing, Swimming, Brewing, Baking, Pottery, Drinking, Forageing etc.)  <P>Well I decide to work on my Forage skill (At 172 now) and thought it would be cool to do it in my home zone. I camped out in front of Felwithe and buffed all the newbies I saw.<P>One person (Andromoda - lvl 1 Enchanter) was just standing there.  I gave her Skin like Diamond, Strength of Earth, Cloroplast, Coat of Spikes and something else I can't remember.<BR>She is still standing there so I say, "Go attack something, it can't hurt you now."<P>She runs out and attacks a bat.  The bat takes one swing and *poof* it's dead.  She runs back absolutly amazed.  I stick around until she hits level 2.  I was going to log out for the night but finally understood that she was a *complete* novice so I took pity on her and showed her the vendor for backpacks, her spells, showed her how to know which cloths would 'fit' her.  Then gave her some food, cash, and a walrus tooth.  (6/22 +3 Str, + 6 Sta, I get dozens of them to drop in a day but they are lore so big deal.)<P>Just before I log out I ask her, very politly, how old she is.  She tells me she is 63.   <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"> hehe a Grandmother.<P>Next day I log in she is back in Felwithe and has found a level 5 cleric who was teaching her how to cast spells and such.  I gave them Group wolf form, Pack Regen, and damage shield. for a couple more hours while they were hunting at Orc Hill.<P>At one point I saw a shout for someone who was willing to pay 50pp for a DL port.  I told her I was going to port someone and that I would be right back.  She says "Can I go?  It sounds like fun?"  I told her "Maybe when you get up a few more levels I'll take you to a few of the other zones."  She was very dissappointed, but I didn't want her death on my hands.<P>Last night I run into her again and she says that she doesn't care if she dies, porting sounds like a lot of fun.  So I invis, see invis, and Buff like crazy, then we go on a world tour of Norrath.  She loved the polly-wog looking things in Freerrot.<P>One other thing I found to be a heck of a lot of fun.  Take off the /anon tag and just wait to see what happens.  Usually you don't have to wait more than 5 minutes before you get a tell from someone who is desparate for some kind of help.  I have had many wonderful adventures this way but also completely understand why I must be /role when I don't want to be disturbed.<P>All this playing has given me the energy to work on getting out of this hell level.<P>Of couse I will be doing a lot more questing, and working on my skills and a lot less leveling now but I think that is a good thing.
</FONT>
