I'm not fully non-KOS yet Ghall.   <IMG SRC="frown.gif" border="0">  I'm still KOS to the frost giants. But, by hunting in Skyshrine you aren't losing ANY Thurgadin faction.  I'll do some research and find out for you what kinda vendors they have, i'm assuming they have trade skill vendors, if not, ports are easy to find.   <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>*****<P>Ok.  Here is how I see it Hieck.  Just my opinion and experiences here, so take it with a grain of salt (or a shot of tequila).    <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Sentient Armor - Drops off Suits of Sentient Armor in Wakening Lands<BR>Great armor for Shadowknights, used to be fairly easy to get.  Problem is... The "suits" are now immune to fear, so no more fear kiting.  They are a awfully annoying, having around 6-8k hit points if I remember correctly.  Add in the facts that you can get exp off them in the mid 50s AND they drop quest related gems, and that means they are camped by groups pretty much nonstop.  If you thought fighting the Holgresh was tough, you ain't seen nothing yet.    <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0">  Gotta have at least 1 good tank, preferably 2, and a good cleric.  Drops of armor are a little more common than Guardian armor, but not by much.<P>Sentry Armor - Drops off named Sentries in Skyshrine<BR>One of the best armors around for chain classes.  As you've already seen, it can be tough to get a camp, and the drops aren't all that common.  They also hit damn hard.    <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0">  These guys are pretty easy to solo as a high-level necro, but normally require at least 1 tank, 1 cleric, 1 other.  To safely single pull without harmony, puller should be 49th or higher.   Should be good exp for the alpha group however, and drops are more common in the "courtyard" aka "pool room".<P>Guardian Armor - Drops off named Guardians AND rarely off Named Sentries in Skyshrine<BR>Pretty much the same as the Sentry Armor information.<P>All in all, not being a shadowknight, I'm not sure how much INT is really a concern for them.  I mean, I know they can cast spells and stuff, but aren't melee stats more important?  <P>I feel that the sentient armor would be the hardest of these three to obtain.  Plus, by hunting in Skyshrine, you get the added bones of potentially getting a drop that ANYbody in your group can use.  Chain armor, plate armor, 2 types of robes, Focused Ethereal weapons, Guardian Sword, Small Coin Purse, cash, and sapphires all drop in this zone.  Sentients drop next to no cash, rarely SK only armor, and even more rarely quest gems.  Once "alpha" group gets into the high 40's I think the sentients might be a good place to gain exp, gems, and some SK armor.<P>[ July 27, 2001: Message edited by: Lownar/Kalaan/Sendil ]<p>[ July 27, 2001: Message edited by: Lownar/Kalaan/Sendil ]<P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 55th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Rakasak - 19th Level Monk<BR>Bertox. Server
